<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zapotec civilization</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zapotecs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zapotec civilization arose in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-oaxaca">Valley of Oaxaca</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, where from about 500 BCE Monte Albán became one of the first cities and states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesoamerica">Mesoamerica</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zapotecs">Zapotecs</a> developed one of the earliest writing systems in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, built temple and palace complexes and buried their nobles in painted tombs. After Monte Albán declined they lived in smaller kingdoms such as Zaachila, Mitla and Tehuantepec, and Zapotec languages are still spoken today.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zapotec-civilization.jpg" alt="Zapotec civilization" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yavidaxiu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zapotecos.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
